From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iván Ruiz <iruizl2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:40:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2159/2160] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p64100-microsoft-denali: Drop
 the fused-off CPU7 and CPU11

The Snapdragon X Plus X1P-64-100 in the LCD Surface Pro 11 has 10
cores: the last core of the second and third clusters is fused off.
hamoa.dtsi describes all 12, so every boot logs

  psci: failed to boot CPU7 (-22)
  psci: failed to boot CPU11 (-22)

and those CPUs stay listed in possible, present and every cluster's
related_cpus. The firmware's ACPI MADT, which Windows uses, lists the
GICC entries for MPIDR 0x10300 and 0x20300 as disabled.

Delete both CPUs, their PSCI power domains and their cpu-map entries.
This is done for this board rather than in an X1P-64-100 SoC dtsi
until it is confirmed that every part fuses off the same two cores.

Fixes: 0d72ccaa1e84 ("arm64: dts: qcom: Add support for X1-based Surface Pro 11")
Link: https://github.com/GeneralPawz/linux-sp11/issues/1
Assisted-by: LLM

---
 .../dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts     | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
index e18444532..d73ba028f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@
 #include "hamoa.dtsi"
 #include "x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi"
 
+/*
+ * The X1P-64-100 has 10 cores: the last core of the second and third
+ * clusters is fused off, and PSCI refuses to start them (-EINVAL), as the
+ * firmware's MADT, which leaves them disabled, tells Windows.
+ */
+/delete-node/ &cpu7;
+/delete-node/ &cpu11;
+/delete-node/ &cpu_pd7;
+/delete-node/ &cpu_pd11;
+
 / {
 	model = "Microsoft Surface Pro 11th Edition (LCD)";
 	compatible = "microsoft,denali-lcd", "microsoft,denali",
@@ -23,6 +33,14 @@ backlight: backlight {
 	};
 };
 
+&cpu_map_cluster2 {
+	/delete-node/ core3;
+};
+
+&{/cpus/cpu-map/cluster1} {
+	/delete-node/ core3;
+};
+
 &panel {
 	backlight = <&backlight>;
 };
-- 
